PART 17 — DEVELOPMENT ORDER

Use this order to minimize regressions.

Phase A — Establish the baseline

1. Read and map the relevant architecture.
2. Run existing tests.
3. Document current attack input and cancellation behavior.
4. Identify the relevant invariants.
5. Identify obsolete specifications and tests that will intentionally change.

Do not begin with arbitrary hitbox changes.

Phase B — Implement Combo Assist queued follow-ups

1. Implement correct alternate resolution.
2. Add one queue per human player.
3. Accept repeated-button presses within the defined window.
4. Preserve the current animation.
5. Detect natural completion.
6. Process the follow-up through normal action eligibility.
7. Implement queue invalidation.
8. Integrate Combat Assist.
9. Update tests and documentation.

Finish and validate this phase before expanding the change.

Phase C — Improve ordinary attack buffering

1. Evaluate the existing 0.15-second duration.
2. Introduce the 0.20-second candidate.
3. Preserve or explicitly separate Dash-buffer timing.
4. Test buffer conflicts and expiry.
5. Verify no accidental delayed execution.
6. Update tests and documentation.

Phase D — Audit responsiveness and accidental cancellations

1. Reproduce startup-cancellation problems.
2. Measure the effects of the new Combo Assist queue.
3. Preserve advanced cancellation freedom.
4. Implement only additional improvements justified by evidence.

Phase E — Audit hitbox alignment and Combat Assist

1. Test common attacks across the four playable fighters.
2. Identify genuinely inaccurate collision geometry.
3. Apply small move-specific corrections where justified.
4. Test movement and stage interactions.
5. Verify the changes do not create excessive reach or unintended balance changes.

Phase F — Refine presentation

1. Add restrained queued-action feedback if useful.
2. Improve misleading availability feedback where warranted.
3. Preserve UI performance.
4. Update both languages.
5. Check keyboard, controller, and touch behavior.

Phase G — Complete regression testing

1. Run focused tests.
2. Run all tests.
3. Verify deterministic simulation.
4. Inspect all changed files.
5. Check documented behavior.
6. Report the final results.

