PART 18 — STRICTLY PROHIBITED SHORTCUTS

Do not:

* Reduce CPU difficulty.
* Adjust CPU reactions or strategy.
* Remove hitboxes from any attacks.
* Make every attack connect automatically.
* Add aim assist to all projectiles.
* Teleport fighters to guarantee hits.
* Restart active attacks from repeated presses.
* Allow unlimited combo buffering.
* Create infinite automatic combos.
* Remove all attack recovery.
* Make different moves share one global cooldown.
* Reduce the current repeat cooldown without explicit justification.
* Bypass long cooldowns through Combo Assist.
* Change damage tiers.
* Remove knockback or Launch Point.
* Add unblockable attacks.
* Remove Shield or Deflect.
* Make all fighters play identically.
* Add per-fighter universal movement values.
* Hide intentional mechanic changes from the product specification.
* Delete tests simply because the redesign makes them fail.
* Fake missing animation frames.
* Break custom controller layouts.
* Ignore mobile controls.
* Add nondeterministic gameplay timers.
* Put new combat logic exclusively into UI components.
* Edit character_rule.
* Refactor unrelated systems without a concrete reason.

Do not confuse making combat easier to control with making the entire game easier to win.

The former is the objective.

CPU balancing will come later.

